From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blogerandrey-ux <blogerandrey-ux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:04:17 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] Add ClientHello controls for reproducing other TLS stacks

This patch adds four client-only knobs, all off by default:

1. SSL_set_extension_order: send ClientHello extensions in an explicit
   order of codepoints. Unlisted extensions follow in the default order;
   GREASE, padding and pre_shared_key keep their positions. Takes
   precedence over SSL_set_permute_extensions.

2. SSL_set_record_size_limit: offer record_size_limit (RFC 8449). A limit
   returned by the server caps the plaintext of records we send.

3. SSL_set_delegated_credential_sigalgs: offer delegated_credential
   (RFC 9345) with the given signature algorithms. Signalling only; a
   delegated credential in the server's Certificate fails the handshake.

4. SSL_set_client_hello_padding: the RFC 7685 padding rule of earlier
   BoringSSL versions (ClientHellos of 256..511 bytes padded to 512), as
   still sent by Android's Conscrypt.

Together these let a BoringSSL client reproduce the ClientHello of NSS
(Firefox) and of older BoringSSL builds byte for byte.
